    <tags>agliteterm terminal ai agent console conpty win32 portable lightweight</tags>
    <summary>A tiny native Windows terminal for AI coding agents</summary>
    <description>
agliteterm is a minimal Windows terminal for old or low-RAM machines: one small C++ exe
(Win32/WTL, **no .NET runtime**) over the same Rust emulator core and pty-host as
[agwinterm](https://github.com/yeroo/agwinterm), with real native controls instead of
custom-drawn chrome.

- **Agent workflow**: workspaces and sessions with per-session agent status (bold = blocked,
  italic = working), an attention bell that jumps to the next blocked session, flagged sessions,
  unread badges, sidebar drag and drop.
- **Scriptable**: the same newline-JSON control pipe as agwinterm, speaking the `agwintermctl`
  dialect — 41 verbs across sessions, workspaces, windows and the tree. Shells get the same
  `AGWINTERM_*` environment, so hooks and the agent skill work in both. A shared conformance suite
  runs in **both** repositories' CI, so "same control API" is enforced rather than asserted.
- **Classic Windows**: menu bar, toolbar, TreeView sidebar, status bar; Dark / Light / Classic /
  Auto themes; bundled bitmap fonts (Cozette, Tamzen, Terminus, Spleen, UNSCII, GNU Unifont);
  MS-DOS/EGA palette; a cmd.exe-style Properties dialog.
- **Explains itself**: an always-on log of its own decisions, and `agliteterm --diagnose` for a
  one-shot report.

If your machine can afford it, take agwinterm instead — it is the fuller terminal. agliteterm
exists for the machines that cannot.

This package installs the **portable** build from the official GitHub release (the setup is a
per-user installer, which does not belong in an elevated package manager). The binaries are
unsigned but carry a Sigstore build-provenance attestation
(`gh attestation verify &lt;file&gt; --repo yeroo/agliteterm`).
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/yeroo/agliteterm/releases/tag/v0.17.9</releaseNotes>
